WEBVTT

00:00:00.862 --> 00:00:03.619
This is FlightDeck Desktop on a Mac.

00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:05.534
It's connected to devbox:

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:09.593
a worker machine, where the agents and the code live.

00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:12.400
Let's open a project on the worker.

00:00:17.332 --> 00:00:27.038
Now start a new agent. Every agent gets its own git branch and worktree, so agents can work side by side without getting in each other's way.

00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:32.855
Claude Code starts right in that worktree, on devbox.

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:34.982
Tell it what to build.

00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:45.804
While it works, the sidebar keeps you posted on what each agent is doing.

00:00:48.485 --> 00:00:55.219
Done. The agent sums up what it changed, and the header shows the changes waiting in its worktree.

00:00:55.765 --> 00:01:00.827
To try it, open a terminal in the same worktree, and start the app.

00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:04.949
Then open a browser inside the session.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:09.854
Its requests are made by the worker, so localhost here is devbox.

00:01:10.211 --> 00:01:13.833
Hover a note, and there's the new delete button.

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:18.551
One click, and the note is gone.

00:01:18.551 --> 00:01:19.295
It works.

00:01:19.931 --> 00:01:23.368
Before finishing, ask the agent to commit its work.

00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:29.935
Committed. Now, Finish merges the agent's branch into main.

00:01:31.408 --> 00:01:36.795
FlightDeck asks first: merge into main, then remove the worktree.

00:01:41.327 --> 00:01:49.129
That's the whole loop: an agent on a remote worker, from the first prompt to a change merged into main.
